control Hamon from his grandfather Jonathan?

163
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:26,020
Jonathan? Yes.

164
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:28,538
But why are you speaking of him now?

165
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:33,440
What the hell?

166
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:37,240
I just took the lives of all these men.

167
00:09:37,540 --> 00:09:43,480
And when you lose your life, Jonathan's
grandson will know grief and anger and hate.

168
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:46,397
He will develop a
tremendous hatred for me.

169
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:48,420
No! Straitzo!

170
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:10,510
Straitzo...

171
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:14,637
Have you lost your senses? I haven't.

172
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:17,500
In fact, my thinking is extremely clear.

173
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:22,560
I chose Harmon to forge my body
into something pure and strong.

174
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:28,720
But as I trained, the aging of my
flesh became painfully clear to me.

175
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:34,620
Harmon provides only a small
advantage over ordinary people.

176
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:37,800
It cannot guard against
the process of aging.

177
00:10:38,260 --> 00:10:43,060
In the battle we fought so many
years ago, I secretly admired Dio.

178
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,797
He was powerful.

179
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,100
He was beautiful.

180
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:49,060
He was immortal.

181
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:53,860
I coveted the power
granted by the Stone Mask.

182
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,360
I didn't care who got in the way.

183
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:00,000
You're a twisted traitor, Straitzo.

184
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:05,080
Your blood will now bring me immortality.

185
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:10,837
With you gone, the only ones to know of
the Mask will be Iran and Joseph Joestar.

186
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,480
And once I have disposed of them,

187
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:17,180
I shall learn more of the
mask than Dio ever could.

188
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,460
No, don't do it.

189
00:11:19,660 --> 00:11:23,307
The knowledge you're seeking
could have terrible consequences.

190
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:29,500
Joe, Joe, breathe.

191
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:44,830
Hey, you!

192
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:47,637
Why don't you get a clue
what you're doing, dumbass?

193
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:50,277
Pull your head out of your
butt and see where you are!

194
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:52,280
Now get the hell out of my way!

195
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:56,940
Hello there! What? Didn't hear that!

196
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,256
I can't make it out!

197
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,617
Would you mind repeating all that?

198
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:03,317
I'd like to know what
it was you meant to say.

199
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:05,260
In case I have to pound you.

200
00:12:06,940 --> 00:12:09,058
Jojo, what is it you're doing there?

201
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:13,800
Granny Arena I asked what
you're doing with that man?

202
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:17,740
Well, you see This man is

203
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,680
A taxi

204
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:23,477
This way you don't have to walk so far.

205
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:26,437
Thank you, Jojo You're
such a thoughtful boy!

206
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:29,420
Climb in, Smokey We're going for a ride.

207
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:36,640
The Joestar family Reduced to
a grandmother And her grandson.

208
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:41,460
Over time, I would hear
bits of their past.

209
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:43,800
Granny, really?

210
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:49,277
Speedwagon sent for us, and we came all the
way to New York simply because he asked.

211
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:51,419
But now we find he's not even here?

212
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:53,619
I think his behavior is quite rude.

213
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:57,113
I'm sure that the oil business
requires much of his time.

214
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:04,620
Say, Granny, I'm curious.

215
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:07,828
Was Speedwagon really
Grandpa's best friend?

216
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:10,200
Is that all it was? Come on now.

217
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:11,800
What are you implying?

218
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:13,620
Well, let's see.

219
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,720
He was never married, was he?

220
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:18,597
And you yourself are a widow. Well,

221
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:20,997
it leads me to wonder
if simple friendship was

222
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:23,880
the only relationship
that was going on there.

223
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,580
You rogue you!

224
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:28,080
Sorry! Ow!

225
00:13:28,260 --> 00:13:30,380
I was wrong! Ow! Forgive me!

226
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:33,140
I know Speedwagon is loyal! Ow!

227
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:36,960
The Joestars tended to be short-lived.

228
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:40,760
Granny Arena lost her husband
in an accident at sea.

229
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:44,100
She was pregnant with a son at the time.

230
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:48,660
When he grew up, he married a girl
who would also survive the wreck.

231
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:54,020
They were JoJo's parents, later
claimed by war and disease.

232
00:13:55,880 --> 00:14:02,140
Granny Arena was a gentle and giving woman,
even to punks like me, or anybody else.

233
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:05,805
Maybe it was because she
lived with loneliness.

234
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,380
JoJo was the same.

235
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:12,989
This time, however, his basic
kindness got him into trouble.

236
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,020
Thanks to me.

237
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:18,680
Hey, waiter! Waiter! Yes, sir.

238
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:23,960
Who decided that stinking animal
could be allowed in here, huh? Huh?

239
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:28,477
His smell is ruining my appetite.

240
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:31,297
That kind shouldn't be
allowed in a place like this.

241
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:32,660
I understand, sir.

242
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:35,537
But there's a policy
handed down by management.

243
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:40,180
As long as the check is paid in full,
we happily serve anyone. What was that?

244
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:44,382
You'll happily let beasts like
that do their grazing in here, huh?

245
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:47,220
Guess I'll just be on my way.

246
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:52,730
Jojo?

247
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:54,660
You heard him. Come on.

248
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:57,920
You're not going to tell
me to stop, are you? No.

249
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:00,515
People are entitled to their opinions.

250
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:05,100
But this misbegotten oaf has
given public insult to our friend.

251
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:09,000
Be mindful of the other guests
now, but teach him a lesson.

252
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:14,120
I was hoping you'd say that.

253
